00:25.264 --> 00:28.225
So what's the meaning of
this definite integral?

00:28.225 --> 00:32.648
So the velocity, velocity is
a vector, it has direction,

00:32.648 --> 00:34.923
and you can see when you look up here

00:34.923 --> 00:37.049
that sometimes the velocity is positive

00:37.049 --> 00:39.405
and sometimes it is negative,

00:39.405 --> 00:42.365
and a reasonable interpretation of that

00:42.365 --> 00:44.722
is well this is when she's
walking in one direction

00:44.722 --> 00:47.810
and then that's where
whatever direction we assume

00:47.810 --> 00:49.831
is the positive direction
and this is when she's

00:49.831 --> 00:51.386
walking the other way,

00:51.386 --> 00:54.730
and so she has a positive velocity here

00:54.730 --> 00:56.088
and then she has a negative velocity.

00:56.088 --> 00:58.352
She has some speed in the other direction

00:58.352 --> 01:01.603
and then she has a
positive velocity again.

01:01.603 --> 01:03.704
So if you were to take the
absolute value of this,

01:03.704 --> 01:06.607
if you just cared about the
magnitude of the velocity,

01:06.607 --> 01:08.081
well we're talking about,

01:08.081 --> 01:10.323
we're talking about speed,

01:10.323 --> 01:11.402
but we're not just talking about

01:11.402 --> 01:13.271
the absolute value of velocity,

01:13.271 --> 01:16.208
we're integrating the
absolute value of velocity

01:16.208 --> 01:18.426
over time from time equals zero

01:18.426 --> 01:20.167
to time equals 40.

01:20.167 --> 01:21.885
So if you integrate speed,

01:21.885 --> 01:23.441
if you're saying okay for every

01:23.441 --> 01:27.029
for every little amount of time DT

01:27.029 --> 01:28.991
she has some speed,

01:28.991 --> 01:31.684
well that's going to give you
the distance that she travels.

01:31.684 --> 01:33.971
So the distance remember,
is the difference

01:33.971 --> 01:35.806
between distance and displacement

01:35.806 --> 01:38.824
is displacement you can
think of as the net distance

01:38.824 --> 01:41.483
it takes if you go back
and forth a bunch of times

01:41.483 --> 01:43.062
it's going to add up to the distance,

01:43.062 --> 01:45.465
but they're going to net out
with respect to each other

01:45.465 --> 01:46.591
in displacement.

01:46.591 --> 01:49.389
So this right over is going
to give us the total distance,

01:49.389 --> 01:54.389
not displacement, that she
travels over those 40 minutes.

01:54.893 --> 01:57.168
If there was no absolute value sign here

01:57.168 --> 01:59.548
then we'd be talking
about the displacement

01:59.548 --> 02:01.522
and so let me write that.

02:01.522 --> 02:03.867
So this integral from zero to 40

02:03.867 --> 02:07.350
absolute value V of T DT

02:07.350 --> 02:12.350
is the total distance

02:13.666 --> 02:16.963
distance she travels

02:16.963 --> 02:18.328
she travels

02:19.483 --> 02:21.062
over the 40 minutes

02:21.062 --> 02:25.649
over the 40, over the 40 minutes,

02:25.649 --> 02:29.144
remember our unit of
time here is in minutes.

02:29.144 --> 02:30.466
All right.

02:30.466 --> 02:34.007
So using correct units and so this is

02:34.007 --> 02:35.528
and so the units,

02:35.528 --> 02:37.143
let me write it this way.

02:37.143 --> 02:38.663
Is a total distance she travels

02:38.663 --> 02:40.021
over the 40 minutes.

02:40.021 --> 02:42.841
The units are meters.

02:42.841 --> 02:46.710
The units are meters,

02:46.710 --> 02:49.810
are meters.

02:49.810 --> 02:50.949
All right,

02:50.949 --> 02:53.329
now this says approximate
the value of that integral

02:53.329 --> 02:55.044
using a right Riemann sum

02:55.044 --> 02:57.865
with the four subintervals
